that license. It does not replace or weaken the licenses, copyright, trademark
rights, end-user terms, or other conditions that apply to third-party works.

Required platforms and dependencies
-----------------------------------

Cookery Engineering calls, links against, or uses registry/API contracts from:

* Minecraft: Java Edition and Mojang/Microsoft-owned classes, registries,
  resource identifiers, and runtime assets. Minecraft is not distributed
  under this license. The project references Minecraft assets at runtime,
  including the bowl item texture used as a GUI guide.
  Terms: https://www.minecraft.net/eula
* NeoForge (`neoforge`), used as the mod loader and platform API. NeoForge is
  licensed separately, principally under LGPL-2.1.
  Source and license: https://github.com/neoforged/NeoForge
* Immersive Engineering (`immersiveengineering`), a required dependency whose
  multiblock API and implementation classes, energy and inventory utilities,
  recipe serializers, GUI helpers, manual API, render helpers, sounds, models,
  textures, and other runtime resources are called or referenced by this
  add-on. Immersive Engineering is governed by Blu's License of Common Sense.
  Source and license:
  https://github.com/BluSunrize/ImmersiveEngineering/blob/1.21.1/LICENSE
* Kaleidoscope Cookery (`kaleidoscope_cookery`), a required dependency whose
  Stockpot, Rice Bowl, Millstone, Chopping Board, ingredient, item, block, and
  recipe contracts are called or referenced by this add-on. Its code and
  assets/data have separate upstream licenses.
  Source: https://github.com/KaleidoscopeMods/KaleidoscopeCookery

Immersive Engineering-derived material
--------------------------------------

The following material incorporates, adapts, or directly depends on Immersive
Engineering artwork or model material and is distributed only under the
permissions and restrictions of Blu's License of Common Sense, not under the
MIT grant above insofar as it contains upstream material:

* `src/main/resources/assets/cookery_engineering/models/block/multiblock/`
  OBJ/MTL content that incorporates or references IE Mixer, Crusher, treated
  wood, sheetmetal, multiblock-component, or other IE model materials;
* `src/main/resources/assets/cookery_engineering/textures/block/multiblock/`
  textures derived from IE artwork, including `treated_wood_lid.png`;
* the maturation-vessel GUI composition, which samples IE-owned GUI textures
  from the installed dependency at runtime rather than bundling those source
  textures;
* use of IE's Mixer agitator, Mixer and Crusher operating sounds, GUI widgets,
  manual rendering, multiblock rendering, and Projector-facing manual data.

Original additions made by Cookery Engineering contributors remain under the
MIT License where they can be separated from upstream material. Attribution
details are also recorded in `src/main/resources/GUI_ART_CREDITS.md`.

Kaleidoscope Cookery-derived recipe data
----------------------------------------

The files under
`src/main/resources/data/cookery_engineering/recipe/sawmill/kaleidoscope_cookery/`
adapt Kaleidoscope Cookery 1.5.0 Chopping Board recipes to Immersive
Engineering's Sawmill format. Those adapted data files are licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), not MIT.

Original data copyright (c) 2025, Kaleidoscope Official Production Team.
Changes: recipe type, processing-energy fields, and IE sawmill output fields
were added while preserving the KC ingredients and results.

Upstream asset license:
https://github.com/KaleidoscopeMods/KaleidoscopeCookery/blob/main/LICENSE-ASSETS

CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 legal code:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/legalcode

Further attribution is recorded in
`src/main/resources/RECIPE_COMPAT_CREDITS.md`.

Optional interoperability declarations
--------------------------------------

Cookery Engineering contains conditional data-pack references or compatibility
paths for the following optional projects. Unless explicitly identified above,
their code and asset binaries are not bundled; names, namespaces, registry IDs,
and public interoperability contracts are referenced only when the relevant
mod is installed. Each project remains governed by its own license:

* Farmer's Delight (`farmersdelight`) -- Rich Soil cloche recipes; upstream
  metadata declares MIT.
* Kaleidoscope ChineseFood (`kaleidoscope_chinesefood`) -- eggplant cloche
  recipes; upstream metadata declares MIT for code and CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for
  assets.
* Kaleidoscope Nether (`kaleidoscope_nether`) -- cloche recipes; upstream
  metadata declares MIT.
* Kaleidoscope End (`kaleidoscope_end`) -- cloche recipes; upstream metadata
  declares MIT.
* Youkai's Feast (`youkaisfeasts`) -- cloche recipes; upstream metadata
  declares LGPL-2.1.
* Create (`create`) -- honeycomb cloche recipe; upstream code is MIT and
  upstream assets are All Rights Reserved.
* Immersive Petroleum (`immersivepetroleum`) -- optional Projector consumes
  the multiblock manual data exposed through IE; no compile-time dependency is
  bundled. Upstream metadata declares All Rights Reserved.
* The conventional `c` tag namespace -- cross-mod ingredient tags only; it is
  not a bundled mod or a claim of ownership.

Development tooling
-------------------

The project is built with Java, Gradle, ModDevGradle, and Parchment mappings.
Parchment mappings are CC0-1.0. These tools and their licenses are independent
of the MIT license granted for Cookery Engineering's original material and are
not relicensed by this file.

No reference to a third-party project grants endorsement, ownership, or rights
beyond those supplied by that project's copyright holders and license terms.
